# Project map (cursor-esp32 workspace)

| Repo | What it is |
|------|------------|
| **lego-rover-esp32** | LEGO rover firmware — T-Display-S3 drive board (motors, IMU, wheel ticks, ring, display) + Pro S3 ToF board |
| **lego-rover-ros2** | Rover brain code (ROS 2 Jazzy), synced from the NUC brain `/data/swarm/robot-fleet` — explore, logging |
| **c3-mini-bot** | Small ESP32-C3 swarm bots — thin clients, namespaced topics, fleet via the NUC brain |
| **yoRadio-fusion-pros3** | yoRadio fork — Fusion Pro S3 internet radio, display, MQTT, NeoStatus |
| **BT-A2DP-Source-HiGrow** | Bluetooth A2DP audio source |
| **GIFPlayer** | GIF playback on ESP display |
| **GoL** | Game of Life (display toy) |
| **Magic-8-Ball** / **Magic-GIF-Ball** | Magic 8 ball variants |
| **NFCNoisy** | NFC-triggered noise toy |
| **lego-roverquest** | Rover-related experiment/quest code |

## Fleet architecture

- **NUC brain** `192.168.3.172` = ROS 2 Jazzy in Docker (`/data/swarm/robot-fleet`) + one micro-ROS agent UDP **8888**.
- Each bot = **thin ESP client** (motors/servos, sensors, local safety, WiFi micro-ROS).
- **0** Rover (`/rover/…`), **1** Roby (`/bot1/…`), **2** Tracker (`/bot2/…`), **4** Beaper (WIP).

